 ## Background
-The integration of parametric human models like SMPL with 3D Gaussian Splatting emerged to address the limitations of unstructured Gaussian representations in animatable avatar reconstruction. Early methods struggled with structural integrity and pose generalization when using purely implicit or explicit Gaussian fields without geometric priors [S1, 1477-gaussian-avatars.md, 1482-relightable-gaussian-codec-avatars.md]. The SMPL model provides a well-established rig and topology, allowing for efficient rigid deformation via LBS [S1, 1480-3dgs-avatar.md, 6157-animatable-gaussians.md, 11805-full-body-avatar-modeling.md]. The addition of non-rigid deformation networks (MLPs) allows the system to capture complex cloth dynamics and body shape variations that LBS alone cannot represent [S1, 1480-3dgs-avatar.md, 6157-animatable-gaussians.md, 11805-full-body-avatar-modeling.md]. This hybrid approach has become a standard for high-fidelity, animatable human avatars in differentiable rendering pipelines [S1, 1479-gaussian-avatar.md, 1480-3dgs-avatar.md, 6157-animatable-gaussians.md, 11653-uv-based-motion-parameterization.md, 11805-full-body-avatar-modeling.md].
+The integration of parametric human models like SMPL with 3D Gaussian Splatting emerged to address the limitations of unstructured Gaussian representations in animatable avatar reconstruction. Early methods struggled with pose generalization and structural integrity. The SMPL-based approach leverages the well-established rig of SMPL to provide a strong geometric prior, allowing Gaussians to be deformed consistently across poses [S1, 1477-gaussian-avatars.md, 1482-relightable-gaussian-codec-avatars.md]. This family has evolved from simple rigid skinning to complex hybrid models incorporating non-rigid residual fields, UV-based parameterizations, and feedforward networks for real-time inference [S1, 1479-gaussian-avatar.md, 1480-3dgs-avatar.md, 6157-animatable-gaussians.md, 11653-uv-based-motion-parameterization.md, 11805-full-body-avatar-modeling.md].
 
